1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
1.1 Executive Summary
Build a production-ready Chrome Extension that intelligently extracts comprehensive job listing data from any job board website. The extension must combine crawling (URL discovery) and scraping (data extraction) techniques to achieve universal compatibility across major job platforms including LinkedIn, Indeed, Glassdoor, Monster, ZipRecruiter, and company career pages. The solution must feature a beautiful, functional UI that provides real-time feedback, extraction progress visualization, and seamless data export capabilities.
1.2 Core Objectives
	•	Universal Compatibility: Design a site-agnostic extraction engine that adapts to different DOM structures, URL patterns, and anti-bot measures across 50+ job board platforms without hardcoding specific selectors for each site.
	•	Comprehensive Data Extraction: Extract all relevant job metadata including title, company name, company domain, location (with geocoding support), full description, original URL, date posted, employment type, salary range (with currency normalization), and application status.
	•	Intelligent Crawling: Implement depth-controlled crawling that discovers job listings from listing pages, follows pagination, handles infinite scroll, and respects robots.txt directives while avoiding duplicate extractions.
	•	Beautiful User Interface: Create a modern, responsive UI with glassmorphism design, smooth animations, real-time progress indicators, job preview cards, filtering capabilities, and intuitive data management features.
	•	Robust Error Handling: Implement comprehensive error recovery, retry mechanisms with exponential backoff, rate limiting compliance, and graceful degradation when extraction partially fails.
